    "MLS",
    "Major&nbsp;League&nbsp;Soccer&nbsp;is&nbsp;divided&nbsp;into&nbsp;Eastern&nbsp;and&nbsp;Western&nbsp;Conferences,&nbsp;with&nbsp;15&nbsp;teams&nbsp;in&nbsp;each&nbsp;competing.&nbsp;Match&nbsp;points&nbsp;are&nbsp;calculated&nbsp;as&nbsp;follows:&nbsp;3&nbsp;points&nbsp;for&nbsp;a&nbsp;win,&nbsp;0&nbsp;points&nbsp;for&nbsp;a&nbsp;loss,&nbsp;and&nbsp;1&nbsp;point&nbsp;each&nbsp;for&nbsp;a&nbsp;draw.&nbsp;Teams&nbsp;are&nbsp;ultimately&nbsp;ranked&nbsp;by&nbsp;total&nbsp;points.&nbsp;Should&nbsp;teams&nbsp;be&nbsp;level&nbsp;on&nbsp;points,&nbsp;the&nbsp;standings&nbsp;are&nbsp;determined&nbsp;by&nbsp;the&nbsp;number&nbsp;of&nbsp;wins.&nbsp;If&nbsp;wins&nbsp;remain&nbsp;equal,&nbsp;the&nbsp;goal&nbsp;difference&nbsp;is&nbsp;considered.&nbsp;Should&nbsp;goal&nbsp;difference&nbsp;still&nbsp;be&nbsp;identical,&nbsp;the&nbsp;total&nbsp;goals&nbsp;scored&nbsp;are&nbsp;used&nbsp;to&nbsp;separate&nbsp;the&nbsp;teams.&nbsp;The&nbsp;MLS&nbsp;Cup&nbsp;champions&nbsp;qualify&nbsp;for&nbsp;the&nbsp;CONCACAF&nbsp;Champions&nbsp;League.&nbsp;Canadian&nbsp;MLS&nbsp;clubs&nbsp;are&nbsp;ineligible&nbsp;for&nbsp;direct&nbsp;CONCACAF&nbsp;Champions&nbsp;League&nbsp;qualification&nbsp;and&nbsp;must&nbsp;instead&nbsp;compete&nbsp;in&nbsp;the&nbsp;Canadian&nbsp;Championship&nbsp;for&nbsp;a&nbsp;spot.&nbsp;Should&nbsp;a&nbsp;Canadian&nbsp;club&nbsp;win&nbsp;the&nbsp;Canadian&nbsp;Championship,&nbsp;the&nbsp;CONCACAF&nbsp;Champions&nbsp;League&nbsp;qualification&nbsp;spot&nbsp;is&nbsp;awarded&nbsp;to&nbsp;the&nbsp;MLS&nbsp;Cup&nbsp;runners-up.<br/><br/>The&nbsp;play-offs&nbsp;are&nbsp;conducted&nbsp;across&nbsp;Eastern&nbsp;and&nbsp;Western&nbsp;Conferences,&nbsp;comprising&nbsp;the&nbsp;First&nbsp;Round,&nbsp;Semi-finals,&nbsp;Conference&nbsp;Finals,&nbsp;and&nbsp;MLS&nbsp;Cup&nbsp;(the&nbsp;Championship&nbsp;Final).&nbsp;Eighteen&nbsp;teams&nbsp;participate:&nbsp;the&nbsp;top&nbsp;seven&nbsp;from&nbsp;each&nbsp;conference's&nbsp;regular&nbsp;season&nbsp;qualify&nbsp;directly&nbsp;for&nbsp;the&nbsp;First&nbsp;Round.&nbsp;The&nbsp;eighth&nbsp;and&nbsp;ninth-placed&nbsp;teams&nbsp;from&nbsp;each&nbsp;conference&nbsp;contest&nbsp;a&nbsp;play-off&nbsp;match&nbsp;for&nbsp;the&nbsp;remaining&nbsp;First&nbsp;Round&nbsp;spot.&nbsp;The&nbsp;play-offs&nbsp;commence&nbsp;on&nbsp;22nd&nbsp;October&nbsp;and&nbsp;conclude&nbsp;on&nbsp;7th&nbsp;December.<br/><br/>First&nbsp;Round&nbsp;Playoffs:&nbsp;The&nbsp;format&nbsp;is&nbsp;best-of-three&nbsp;matches.&nbsp;Should&nbsp;a&nbsp;match&nbsp;end&nbsp;in&nbsp;a&nbsp;draw&nbsp;after&nbsp;90&nbsp;minutes,&nbsp;it&nbsp;proceeds&nbsp;directly&nbsp;to&nbsp;a&nbsp;penalty&nbsp;shootout&nbsp;to&nbsp;determine&nbsp;the&nbsp;winner.&nbsp;No&nbsp;aggregate&nbsp;score&nbsp;is&nbsp;carried&nbsp;over&nbsp;from&nbsp;this&nbsp;round.<br/><br/>Quarter-finals,&nbsp;Semi-finals&nbsp;(Conference&nbsp;Finals),&nbsp;and&nbsp;Finals&nbsp;(Championship):&nbsp;These&nbsp;are&nbsp;single-elimination&nbsp;matches.&nbsp;Should&nbsp;a&nbsp;match&nbsp;end&nbsp;in&nbsp;a&nbsp;draw&nbsp;after&nbsp;regulation&nbsp;time,&nbsp;it&nbsp;proceeds&nbsp;to&nbsp;extra&nbsp;time.&nbsp;Should&nbsp;extra&nbsp;time&nbsp;also&nbsp;end&nbsp;in&nbsp;a&nbsp;draw,&nbsp;a&nbsp;penalty&nbsp;shootout&nbsp;is&nbsp;conducted.",
